# Markdown rules

> Applies to: `**/*.md`, `**/*.mdx`, `**/*.md.scaffold`
> Toolchain version: Node 20 (for linters/formatters)  ·  Package manager: pnpm

## Commands (run from repo root)

| Purpose        | Command                                   |
| -------------- | ----------------------------------------- |
| Install deps   | `pnpm install`                            |
| Build          | N/A                                       |
| Run (dev)      | N/A                                       |
| Test (all)     | `pnpm markdownlint "**/*.md"`             |
| Test (single)  | `pnpm markdownlint path/to/file.md`       |
| Lint           | `pnpm markdownlint "**/*.md"`             |
| Format         | `pnpm prettier --write "**/*.md"`         |
| Typecheck      | N/A                                       |

- `prettier` is **authoritative** for formatting — don't hand-wrap or hand-align; run it.
- Also check links before declaring done (e.g. `pnpm markdown-link-check`), and run lint (see root DoD).

## Style & structure

- Linter/formatter config lives in `.markdownlint.json` and `.prettierrc` — don't override inline unless the config says so.
- One `# H1` per file; don't skip heading levels (`##` → `####` is not allowed).
- Prefer `-` for unordered lists and `1.` for ordered lists; keep list style consistent within a file.
- Use fenced code blocks with a language tag (```bash, ```python), not indented blocks.
- Keep files focused; per root rule, split long docs into linked files rather than one giant page (the LOC cap targets code, but keep prose navigable too).
- Reference other rules/docs by relative link, matching the root "explicit pointer" convention.

## Errors & logging

- N/A for prose. If a doc documents error handling, it must match the root "fail fast, no silent fallback" rule.

## Testing

- "Tests" = lint + link check. Run `markdownlint` and a link checker over changed files.
- New docs ship lint-clean and link-clean. Don't disable a rule inline (`<!-- markdownlint-disable -->`) just to pass — fix the content or justify the exception in the config.

## Dependencies

- Add tooling via `pnpm add -D <pkg>`; commit `pnpm-lock.yaml`.
- Pin versions via the lockfile; prefer maintained, permissively licensed tools.
- Qualify a new dependency with the user before adding it (root rule).
- Do not hand-edit generated docs: API reference output, `CHANGELOG.md` when tool-generated, `node_modules/`.

## Language-specific gotchas

- Relative links break when files move — verify link targets exist after renames/moves.
- Trailing whitespace creates hard line breaks in some renderers; let the formatter strip it.
- Fenced code blocks inside code blocks need a longer fence (````) or they close early.
- HTML in Markdown renders differently across GitHub / MDX / static-site generators — keep it minimal and portable.
- `.scaffold` files are Markdown too: lint them, but they must **not** be auto-activated (see root project goal).
